"Shows a resource-feasible project chain and strategically placed buffers that protect completion from variation.\n\nUse when: Coordinate a project constrained by both dependencies and shared resources. Make project and feeding-buffer protection visible.\n\nAvoid when: The team only needs a precedence network and has not resolved resource conflicts.\n\nVisual grammar: Scheduled activities reflect both logical and resource dependencies. The critical chain identifies the controlling resource-feasible sequence. Project and feeding buffers appear as distinct protective time regions.\n\nBuild: Create a dependency schedule and resolve shared-resource conflicts. Identify the resulting critical chain using declared task-time assumptions. Place and document project and feeding buffers under the chosen method.\n\nCheck: The critical chain accounts for resource constraints. Buffers are distinct from productive task work. Buffer placement and duration follow an explicit, reviewable policy.\n\nPitfalls: Calling the critical path a critical chain without checking resources. Adding buffer time on top of unchanged hidden task safety.\n\nExample: A fit-out project shares one specialist across tasks; its resource-feasible chain is protected by a project buffer and feeding buffers.\n\nAlternatives: Activity network, Gantt chart."
